&lt;h2 id="branches--those-kind-of-branches"&gt;Branches &amp;ndash; Those Kind of Branches?
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;We already covered Git&amp;rsquo;s daily workflow under a single branch in the last section. Notably, we said &amp;ldquo;single branch,&amp;rdquo; which naturally implies that Git supports &amp;ndash; and encourages &amp;ndash; the use of multiple branches. So what is a branch, exactly?&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>(Maybe) a Git Tutorial? Part One</title><link>https://a-moment096.github.io/en/posts/shell_note/git_how/git_1/</link><pubDate>Mon, 28 Jul 2025 22:49:16 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://a-moment096.github.io/en/posts/shell_note/git_how/git_1/</guid><description>&lt;img src="https://a-moment096.github.io/images/Tatara-Kogasa.jpg" alt="Featured image of post (Maybe) a Git Tutorial? Part One" /&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Git is really great, but Git&amp;rsquo;s commands are really complicated. Let me do a quick write-up &amp;ndash; might as well call it a tutorial~&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
